  "title": "Erdős Problem #970",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $h(k)$ be Jacobsthal's function, defined to as the minimal $m$ such that, if $n$ has at most $k$ prime factors, then in any set of $m$ consecutive integers there exists an integer coprime to $n$. Determine the order of magnitude of $h(k)$. In particular, is it true that $ h(k) \\ll k^2? $ ",
